          "type": "text",
          "text": "[2609.02850] Chern flow and Chern moment algebras (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02850)\n【turn128250view0】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02850\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 2 Sep 2026 (【5†v1】), last revised 13 Sep 2026 (this version, v4)]\nL9: # Title:Chern flow and Chern moment algebras\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang】, 【7†Zhenpeng Wang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Chern flow and Chern moment algebras, by Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang and Zhenpeng Wang\nL14: \nL15: 【8†View PDF】 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:We construct realizable-volume models over every field for the factorial normalizations of homogeneous Lascoux, Lascoux-atom, and positive Grothendieck packets, including their minimal homogenizations and layers. In particular, the construction realizes the factorial normalizations of all Schubert and key polynomials and of the minimal sign-corrected homogeneous Grothendieck polynomials.\nL17: The normalized polynomials are Lorentzian, and the ordinary supports are the lattice points of integral generalized polymatroids. On a Bott--Samelson tower, row and co-row filtrations assemble the local factors into globally generated bundles; a creation-state graph absorbs the remaining kernel factors by Chern flow.\nL18: > We also construct intrinsic algebras of joint Chern moments. Positive inverse-Chern presentations give these algebras Hard Lefschetz and Hodge--Riemann relations, and supply source-level Hodge completions of the packets. For globally generated tropical toric bundles in the sense of Kaveh--Manon, finite generating witnesses and matroid duality provide the presentations required by Larson--Partida's theorem, without representability.\nL19: These constructions yield joint Chern-number inequalities, nonvanishing polymatroids, and equality criteria.\nL20: Comments:  | 74 pages. Comments are welcome\nL21: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO); Algebraic Geometry (math.AG)\nL22: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 14M15 (Primary) 05E14, 05E05, 14C17 (Secondary)\nL23: Cite as:  | 【10†arXiv:2609.02850】 [math.CO]\nL24:    | (or 【11†arXiv:2609.02850v4】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL25:    | 【12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.02850†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Zhenpeng Wang [【13†view email】]\nL29: 【5†[v1]】 Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:35:09 UTC (45 KB)\nL30: 【14†[v2]】 Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:55:27 UTC (50 KB)\nL31: 【15†[v3]】 Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:59:19 UTC (79 KB)\nL32: [v4] Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:00:51 UTC (72 KB)\nL33: \nL34: Full-text links:\nL35: \nL36: ## Access Paper:\nL37: \nL38: View a PDF of the paper titled Chern flow and Chern moment algebras, by Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang and Zhenpeng Wang\nL39: \nL40:   * 【8†View PDF】\nL41:   * 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL42:   * 【16†TeX Source】\nL43: \nL44: 【17†view license】\nL45: ### Current browse context:\nL46: \nL47: math.CO\nL48: \nL49: 【18†< prev】   |   【19†next >】\nL50: \nL51: 【20†new】 | 【21†recent】 | 【22†2026-09】\nL52: \nL53: Change to browse by:\nL54: \nL55: 【23†math】\nL56: 【24†math.AG】\nL57: \nL58: ### References & Citations\nL59: \nL60:   * 【25†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL61:   * 【26†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL62:   * 【27†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL63: \nL64: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL65: \nL66: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL67: \nL68: [Button: ×]\nL69: \nL70: loading...\nL71: \nL72: Data provided by:\nL73: \nL74: ### Bookmark\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL77: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer