perimental projects with community collaborators\nL154: \nL155: arXivLabs is a framework that allows collaborators to develop and share new arXiv features directly on our website.\nL156: \nL157: Both individuals and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL158: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? 【43†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org】.\nL159: \nL160: 【44†Which authors of this paper are endorsers?】 | Disable MathJax (【45†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL161: \nL162: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, 【46†member institutions†info.arxiv.org】, , and all contributors.\nL163: 【47†About†info.arxiv.org】 · 【48†Help†info.arxiv.org】 · 【49†Contact†info.arxiv.org】 · 【50†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org】 · 【51†Copyright†info.arxiv.org】 · 【52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org】 · 【53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org】 · 【54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org】\nL164: \nL165: Major funding support from\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2506.22415] Linear operators preserving volume polynomials (https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.22415)\n【turn128250view1】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.22415\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Algebraic Geometry\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 27 Jun 2025]\nL9: # Title:Linear operators preserving volume polynomials\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Lukas Grund】, 【6†June Huh】, 【7†Mateusz Michałek】, 【8†Hendrik Süss】, 【9†Botong Wang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Linear operators preserving volume polynomials, by Lukas Grund and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【10†View PDF】 【11†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:Volume polynomials measure the growth of Minkowski sums of convex bodies and of tensor powers of positive line bundles on projective varieties. We show that Aluffi's covolume polynomials are precisely the polynomial differential operators that preserve volume polynomials, reflecting a duality between homology and cohomology. We then present several applications to matroid theory.\nL17: Subjects:  | Algebraic Geometry (math.AG); Combinatorics (math.CO)\nL18: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 14C17, 05B35, 52A39\nL19: Cite as:  | 【12†arXiv:2506.22415】 [math.AG]\nL20:    | (or 【13†arXiv:2506.22415v1】 [math.AG] for this version)\nL21:    | 【14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2506.22415†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Botong Wang [【15†view email】]\nL25: [v1] Fri, 27 Jun 2025 17:42:27 UTC (30 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Linear operators preserving volume polynomials, by Lukas Grund and 4 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * 【10†View PDF】\nL34:   * 【11†HTML (experimental)】\nL35:   * 【16†TeX Source】\nL36: \nL37: 【17†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL38: ### Current browse context:\nL39: \nL40: math.AG\nL41: \nL42: 【18†< prev】   |   【19†next >】\nL43: \nL44: 【20†new】 | 【21†recent】 | 【22†2025-06】\nL45: \nL46: Change to browse by:\nL47: \nL48: 【23†math】\nL49: 【24†math.CO】\nL50: \nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * 【25†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL54:   * 【26†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL55:   * 【27†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL6