41:   * Venue\nL142:   * Institution\nL143:   * Topic\nL144: \nL145: [Input] About arXivLabs\nL146: # arXivLabs: experimental projects with community collaborators\nL147: \nL148: arXivLabs is a framework that allows collaborators to develop and share new arXiv features directly on our website.\nL149: \nL150: Both individuals and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL151: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? 【43†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org】.\nL152: \nL153: 【44†Which authors of this paper are endorsers?】 | Disable MathJax (【45†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL154: \nL155: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, 【46†member institutions†info.arxiv.org】, , and all contributors.\nL156: 【47†About†info.arxiv.org】 · 【48†Help†info.arxiv.org】 · 【49†Contact†info.arxiv.org】 · 【50†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org】 · 【51†Copyright†info.arxiv.org】 · 【52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org】 · 【53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org】 · 【54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org】\nL157: \nL158: Major funding support from\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2608.10516] Richardson volume models for skew Schur and skew Schur $P/Q$-functions (https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.10516)\n【turn128250view2】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.10516\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 11 Aug 2026 (【5†v1】), last revised 25 Aug 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Richardson volume models for skew Schur and skew Schur $P/Q$-functions\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang】, 【7†with an Appendix by Zhenpeng Wang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Richardson volume models for skew Schur and skew Schur $P/Q$-functions, by Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【8†View PDF】 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:We identify ordinary skew Schur polynomials and skew Schur $P$-functions as top-degree total-Chern intersection polynomials on Richardson varieties in ordinary and Lagrangian Grassmannians. We then obtain that \\[\nL17: > \\mathcal N(s_{\\lambda/\\mu}),\\qquad\nL18: > \\mathcal N(P_{\\lambda/\\mu}),\\qquad\nL19: > \\mathcal N(Q_{\\lambda/\\mu}) \\] are realizable volume polynomials. This settles the skew-Schur and Schur-$P$ Lorentzian conjectures of Huh--Matherne--Mészáros--St.~Dizier and strengthens the latter to arbitrary skew $P/Q$-functions.\nL20: > The constructions extend to cycle transforms attached to arbitrary irreducible subvarieties of ordinary and Lagrangian Grassmannians.\nL21: Their realizable-volume interpretation yields reverse Khovanskii--Teissier and Lorentzian Hodge--Riemann inequalities for ordinary and shifted tableau multiplicities; exact ordinary skew-Schur support permutahedra and extremal coefficients; the known straight shifted support polytopes with their vertex coefficients; implicit exact permutahedra for arbitrary skew $P/Q$-functions; and weighted-aggregation, covariance, and two-row Littlewood--Richardson consequences.\nL22: > An appendix by Zhenpeng Wang constructs the dual type~$D$ spinor cycle transform and a direct Richardson realization of $Q_{\\lambda/\\mu}$. In characteristic two, compatible very special isogenies induce finite flat radicial morphisms between the ambient Lagrangian and spinor models.\nL23: Their restrictions to the corresponding Richardson varieties have degrees $2^{\\ell(\\lambda)-\\ell(\\mu)}$ and $2^{|\\lambda|-|\\mu|-\\ell(\\lambda)+\\ell(\\mu)}$, and a regular complete-intersection bridge explains the difference between the two projective-bundle shifts.\nL24: Comments:  | Comments welcome!\nL25: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO)\nL26: Cite as:  | 【10†arXiv:2608.10516】 [math.CO]\nL27:    | (or 【11†arXiv:2608.10516v2】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL28:    | 【12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.10516†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL29: ## Submission history\nL30: \nL31: From: Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang [【13†view email】]\nL32: 【5†[v1]】 Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:40:40 UTC (29 KB)\nL33: [v2] Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:48:35 UTC (47 KB)\nL34: \nL35: Full-text links:\nL36: \nL37: ## Access Paper:\nL38: \nL39: View a PDF of the paper titled Richardson volume models for skew Schur and skew Schur $P/Q$-functions, by Khai-Hoan Nguyen-Dang and 1 other authors\nL40: \nL41:   * 【8†View PDF】\nL42:   * 【9†HTML (experimental)】\nL43:   * 【14†TeX Source】\nL44: \nL45: 【15†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL46: ### Current browse context:\nL47: \nL48: math.CO\nL49: \nL50: 【16†< prev】   |   【17†next >】\nL51: \nL52: 【18†new】 | 【19†recent】 | 【20†2026-08】\nL53: \nL54: Change to browse by:\nL55: \nL56: 【21†math】\nL57: \nL58: ### References & Citations\nL59: \nL60:   * 【22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL61:   * 【23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL62:   * 【24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL63: \nL64: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL65: \nL66: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL67: \nL68: [Button: ×]\nL69: \nL70: loading...\nL71: \nL72: Data provided by:\nL73: \nL74: ### Bookmark\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL77: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL80: \nL81: Bibliographic Explorer (【25†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL82: \nL83: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL84: \nL85: Connected Papers (【26†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com】)\nL86: \nL87: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL88: \nL89: Litmaps (【27†What is Lit