of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL158: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? 【40†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org】.\nL159: \nL160: 【41†Which authors of this paper are endorsers?】 | Disable MathJax (【42†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL161: \nL162: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, 【43†member institutions†info.arxiv.org】, , and all contributors.\nL163: 【44†About†info.arxiv.org】 · 【45†Help†info.arxiv.org】 · 【46†Contact†info.arxiv.org】 · 【47†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org】 · 【48†Copyright†info.arxiv.org】 · 【49†Privacy†info.arxiv.org】 · 【50†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org】 · 【51†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org】\nL164: \nL165: Major funding support from\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2608.12266] Normalized skew Schur polynomials are Lorentzian (https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.12266)\n【turn128250view3】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.12266\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Aug 2026]\nL9: # Title:Normalized skew Schur polynomials are Lorentzian\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Philip B. Zhang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Normalized skew Schur polynomials are Lorentzian, by Philip B. Zhang\nL14: \nL15: 【6†View PDF】 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:We prove the conjecture of Huh, Matherne, Mészáros, and St.~Dizier that the normalization of every skew Schur polynomial in finitely many variables is Lorentzian. We first realize every nonzero skew Schur polynomial in finitely many variables as a specialization of a Schubert polynomial and prove that it is dually Lorentzian. The dual Jacobi--Trudi identity then identifies its normalization with the finite dual of a skew Schur polynomial obtained by rectangular complementation.\nL17: As a consequence, skew Kostka numbers satisfy log-concavity inequalities along the root directions.\nL18: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO)\nL19: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 05E05, 05E14\nL20: Cite as:  | 【8†arXiv:2608.12266】 [math.CO]\nL21:    | (or 【9†arXiv:2608.12266v1】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL22:    | 【10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.12266†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Philip B. Zhang [【11†view email】]\nL26: [v1] Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:06:13 UTC (10 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Normalized skew Schur polynomials are Lorentzian, by Philip B. Zhang\nL33: \nL34:   * 【6†View PDF】\nL35:   * 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL36:   * 【12†TeX Source】\nL37: \nL38: 【13†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL39: \nL40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: math.CO\nL43: \nL44: 【14†< prev】   |   【15†next >】\nL45: \nL46: 【16†new】 | 【17†recent】 | 【18†2026-08】\nL47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: 【19†math】\nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * 【20†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL54:   * 【21†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL55:   * 【22†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (【23†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL75: \nL76: [Input] Connected 